ser":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-20T21:56:57-07:00","id":1409468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1408355-scion-homebrew-nemetondevos-revised?p=1409461#post1409461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fascinating! Why 1938? Because of the Superman myth?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never heard of the Superman Myth before, though it sounds interesting. I use that date because I desperately don't like dealing with WWII in the context of Scion and this lets me just side-step it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T04:49:35-07:00","id":1409516,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the sort but extremely productive class. I had not the time to read the book yet, but it\u2019s in the top of the list, and now so is the Lebor Oe In Dea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T05:37:25-07:00","id":1409526,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> I meant the creation of Superman the DC character. A lot of people see superheroes as modern myth.<br /> <br /> Awesome! So in your World World War II never happens because of Scions. Imma maybe use that if I ever do a Scion game.<br /> <br /> Do you use the default dial settings from Mysteries of the World in your game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T08:30:01-07:00","id":1409566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1408355-scion-homebrew-nemetondevos-revised?p=1409526#post1409526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"394\" data-vbnamecard=\"394\">Watcher</a> I meant the creation of Superman the DC character. A lot of people see superheroes as modern myth.<br /> <br /> Awesome! So in your World World War II never happens because of Scions. Imma maybe use that if I ever do a Scion game.<br /> <br /> Do you use the default dial settings from Mysteries of the World in your game?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda. World War II doesn't happen in my games due to large scale Divine Intervention such as Archangel Michael manifesting at his full Legend and manifestations in the Sino-Japanese War. Ultimately it is not because I want to make a good story about it, but because I have run and played in Scion for over a decade now, and there is no good way to get within fifty conceptual miles of WWII without creating some really serious issues within the internal logic of The World or starting to get into some pretty awful places. So, this is just a vague background narrative device I use to side-step it entirely.<br /> <br /> The Setting Dials I use normally rapidly change. Most games I play start off at Iron all around, but the general equilibrium I end up with is Genre: Heroic, Theocentrism: Gold, Titanomachy: Invalid (I deal with Titans on a one-by-one basis, so the Titanomachy setting doesn't do anything for me), Evidence: Gold.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T09:50:43-07:00","id":1409582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1408355-scion-homebrew-nemetondevos-revised?p=1409378#post1409378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A single mass break out is not central to the setting lore anymore. But the core does play with the idea that there is a weakening of the separate prisons of many titans resulting in the escalation of the always brewing cold war status of the Titanomachy at the moment. Basically 2E puts it there if you want it, but it does not DEPEND on it the way 1E did.</div> </div> </div> </div>ooh. ok. and now that you explain it that way, I think I can grow to truly love 2e like I do 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T19:15:36-07:00","id":1409670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1408355-scion-homebrew-nemetondevos-revised?p=1409566#post1409566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda. World War II doesn't happen in my games due to large scale Divine Intervention such as Archangel Michael manifesting at his full Legend and manifestations in the Sino-Japanese War. Ultimately it is not because I want to make a good story about it, but because I have run and played in Scion for over a decade now, and there is no good way to get within fifty conceptual miles of WWII without creating some really serious issues within the internal logic of The World or starting to get into some pretty awful places. So, this is just a vague background narrative device I use to side-step it entirely.<br /> <br /> The Setting Dials I use normally rapidly change. Most games I play start off at Iron all around, but the general equilibrium I end up with is Genre: Heroic, Theocentrism: Gold, Titanomachy: Invalid (I deal with Titans on a one-by-one basis, so the Titanomachy setting doesn't do anything for me), Evidence: Gold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome \ud83d\ude0a. I get the horrible places part, but could you give me an example of how World War II messes with the internal logic of the World?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T19:17:17-07:00","id":1409672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1408355-scion-homebrew-nemetondevos-revised?p=1409582#post1409582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ooh. ok. and now that you explain it that way, I think I can grow to truly love 2e like I do 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e is great. The Titanomachy is still present, but it\u2019s less of a monomyth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-21T19:45:15-07:00","id":1409679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1408355-scion-homebrew-nemetondevos-revised?p=1409670#post1409670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome \ud83d\ude0a. I get the horrible places part, but could you give me an example of how World War II messes with the internal logic of the World?</div> </div> </div> </div>The big challenge is that the internal logical issues are the result of the horrible implications which we saw in how 1e attempted and dropped the ball on approaching it in 1e. 1e realized that if one side of the war had Scions, in order for there to be any sense of similar historical developments, so did the other side. Which then results in saying that an actual real-world God had a Scion of theirs on the wrong side of the war and were thereby complicit in the grotesqueness. This, obviously, is a challenge. By attempting to fit the situation into the context of Scion, horrible implications are invoked. They attempted to side-step it themselves by saying that through possession of The Spear of Longuinus, Hitler's actions were somehow obscured from the deeds of all of the Omniscient, Omnipresent, and Omnipotent deities which is starting to tread the absolutely uncomfortable terrain of saying that deities who are All Knowing are not actually All Knowing, etc.<br /> <br /> So, the issue is ultimately: Scions are monsterously powerful. Not just in terms of physical capacity for violence, but capacity to talk, and change societies with their words. If there were Scions involved, how did the events that unfolded unfold unless the Axis had Scions of their own. And if they did, whose Scions were they and who is thereby complicit.<br /> <br /> I have been playing Scion since I was 15, and it has been over a decade now. I have seen people argue this tooth and nail here and in other places, and honestly, I just have never seen an answer to how to deal with WWII that doesn't get trapped between the Internal Logic and the Horrific Implications. The closest I have seen someone get is saying that there were no Scions or any deities involved at all, which works right until you take into account some Pantheons micromanage every little detail of physics and natural events, which means that those Pantheons would be involved no matter what unless you intend to violate their cosmologic rules.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, World War Two is a testament to us being monsters, and serves as the last breath of empires that were founded on such deeds. It is the capstone in a lot of weird and tricky questions in Scion's version of The World (Did Tenochiclan fall in The World? Did the Disaster at Cajamarca happen in The World? Did the Opium Wars happen in The World? etc etc.) that I have never found a good answer for that doesn't result in suggestions of inaction or involvement on The Bad Side.<br /> <br /> Now, those of you who are reading along and sharpening your words, before this becomes a giant argument as I have seen time, and time and time again about Colonialism and World War Two in The World, I would really rather we not rehash out this argument. We have had it before, we all know nobody is going to come out ahead of it. I'm just answering the question I got asked, I don't want to have this fight again, both because I'm exhausted of having it and because this is a thread to talk about the Nemetondevos, something I have been passionate about since I was a kiddo. I would really appreciate it if we didn't have to have the argument again here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T00:13:58-07:00","id":1409704,"title":"","content":"So, about the Nemetondevos... I admit that when I read the PSP, I had to pause because it was the first time I had heard the word 'cyst' used outside of a medical context. Heck, I didn't even know it had a non-medical use","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T01:10:59-07:00","id":1409713,"title":"","content":"Same, it definitely tripped me up as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T02:07:50-07:00","id":1409722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1408355-scion-homebrew-nemetondevos-revised?p=1409679#post1409679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The big challenge is that the internal logical issues are the result of the horrible implications which we saw in how 1e attempted and dropped the ball on approaching it in 1e. 1e realized that if one side of the war had Scions, in order for there to be any sense of similar historical developments, so did the other side. Which then results in saying that an actual real-world God had a Scion of theirs on the wrong side of the war and were thereby complicit in the grotesqueness. This, obviously, is a challenge. By attempting to fit the situation into the context of Scion, horrible implications are invoked. They attempted to side-step it themselves by saying that through possession of The Spear of Longuinus, Hitler's actions were somehow obscured from the deeds of all of the Omniscient, Omnipresent, and Omnipotent deities which is starting to tread the absolutely uncomfortable terrain of saying that deities who are All Knowing are not actually All Knowing, etc.<br /> <br /> So, the issue is ultimately: Scions are monsterously powerful. Not just in terms of physical capacity for violence, but capacity to talk, and change societies with their words. If there were Scions involved, how did the events that unfolded unfold unless the Axis had Scions of their own. And if they did, whose Scions were they and who is thereby complicit.<br /> <br /> I have been playing Scion since I was 15, and it has been over a decade now. I have seen people argue this tooth and nail here and in other places, and honestly, I just have never seen an answer to how to deal with WWII that doesn't get trapped between the Internal Logic and the Horrific Implications. The closest I have seen someone get is saying that there were no Scions or any deities involved at all, which works right until you take into account some Pantheons micromanage every little detail of physics and natural events, which means that those Pantheons would be involved no matter what unless you intend to violate their cosmologic rules.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, World War Two is a testament to us being monsters, and serves as the last breath of empires that were founded on such deeds. It is the capstone in a lot of weird and tricky questions in Scion's version of The World (Did Tenochiclan fall in The World? Did the Disaster at Cajamarca happen in The World? Did the Opium Wars happen in The World? etc etc.) that I have never found a good answer for that doesn't result in suggestions of inaction or involvement on The Bad Side.<br /> <br /> Now, those of you who are reading along and sharpening your words, before this becomes a giant argument as I have seen time, and time and time again about Colonialism and World War Two in The World, I would really rather we not rehash out this argument. We have had it before, we all know nobody is going to come out ahead of it. I'm just answering the question I got asked, I don't want to have this fight again, both because I'm exhausted of having it and because this is a thread to talk about the Nemetondevos, something I have been passionate about since I was a kiddo. I would really appreciate it if we didn't have to have the argument again here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. Idk any of this. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T06:44:17-07:00","id":1409754,"title":"","content":"If the implications of past events are too toxic,( myself I choose to remember the difference between fact and fancy, but my degree is history,) why not embrace Sci Fi? Set political conflicts on distant worlds. Build sides that each have both flaws and valid points. Both mortals and deities can have legitimate conflicts get out of hand. Noble and decent people can make brutal mistakes. Homer's whole take on the Trojan war involved the idea that the Trojans were in fact nobler than the Greeks but still in the wrong. That kind of complexity could be brought in to the narrative in a sci fi setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T07:13:11-07:00","id":1409758,"title":"","content":"I quite like the Mabon entry and if i ever get to play i'd love to do a scion or incarnate of him.<br /> Am i right to think the mention of a &quot;Shining youth with unshorned hair&quot; is a reference to ... Apollon maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T08:08:40-07:00","id":1409764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1408355-scion-homebrew-nemetondevos-revised?p=1409758#post1409758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I quite like the Mabon entry and if i ever get to play i'd love to do a scion or incarnate of him.<br /> <br /> Am i right to think the mention of a &quot;Shining youth with unshorned hair&quot; is a reference to ... Apollon maybe?</div> </div> </div> </div>You would be correct! I'm not entirely sure of Apollon kept the unshorn hair concept in Rome (it is an epithet referencing youth as young men having their hair cut for the first time is a right of passage into adulthood), but it is in Greece and it tied in with Mabon himself being a young figure, so, I kept it for that mirroring.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T09:22:01-07:00","id":1409774,"title":"","content":"When I finally get to buy the book it will be fun to see who Mabon was. Both because Michael the Arc Angel took over Michaelmas from him and Lucy Patton and Roger Sherman Lewis thought Modred was a warped misreading of him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T09:26:51-07:00","id":1409775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1408355-scion-homebrew-nemetondevos-revised?p=1409774#post1409774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I finally get to buy the book it will be fun to see who Mabon was. Both because Michael the Arc Angel took over Michaelmas from him and Lucy Patton and Roger Sherman Lewis thought Modred was a warped misreading of him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Watcher's Nemetondevos (the version actually featuring Mabon) are free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T10:03:29-07:00","id":1409778,"title":"","content":"I have never heard the suggestion that Maponos / Mabon were the original figures involved in Michaelmas. From what I know of the development of the liturgical calendar and the conversion of Wales, I think the development of Michaelmas takes place in Rome one or two centuries before the solid conversion of Wales under Saint David, and several centuries before the regional Celtic Churches had their religious traditions brought under the control of Rome. Do you know where that suggestion comes from Astromancer? It isn't one I have heard in the course of my studies and am interested in knowing where that's coming from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T10:28:04-07:00","id":1409784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1408355-scion-homebrew-nemetondevos-revised?p=1409764#post1409764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You would be correct! I'm not entirely sure of Apollon kept the unshorn hair concept in Rome (it is an epithet referencing youth as young men having their hair cut for the first time is a right of passage into adulthood), but it is in Greece and it tied in with Mabon himself being a young figure, so, I kept it for that mirroring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woohoo. I get to feel all smart now. \ud83d\ude0a<br /> I really like when a book gives me clues and plot hooks that i can try to figure out.<br /> <br /> So very well done and i'll be hype to see how you develop the nementondevos + TDD expansions once Demigod is done and out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T12:00:53-07:00","id":1409793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1408355-scion-homebrew-nemetondevos-revised?p=1409778#post1409778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have never heard the suggestion that Maponos / Mabon were the original figures involved in Michaelmas. From what I know of the development of the liturgical calendar and the conversion of Wales, I think the development of Michaelmas takes place in Rome one or two centuries before the solid conversion of Wales under Saint David, and several centuries before the regional Celtic Churches had their religious traditions brought under the control of Rome. Do you know where that suggestion comes from Astromancer? It isn't one I have heard in the course of my studies and am interested in knowing where that's coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>All I know is that certain festivals linked to harvest, apples, and blackberries, were linked to Mabon, were held just after the fall equinox, and the customs of those festivals got rolled into Michaelmas. The authors I read may have made to many assumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T12:12:55-07:00","id":1409795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1408355-scion-homebrew-nemetondevos-revised?p=1409793#post1409793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I know is that certain festivals linked to harvest, apples, and blackberries, were linked to Mabon, were held just after the fall equinox, and the customs of those festivals got rolled into Michaelmas. The authors I read may have made to many assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just talked to a friend of mine who is a retired Professor on the topic and he says it is a series of chained associations. The use of Mabon as the source for an autumnal festival in Wicca is entirely a product of the last century. Later, people claimed that, this festival was consumed by Michaelmas were taking this modern festival and inserting it into the past into a period of Welsh history we lack any historical sources for. (The name Mabon doesn't even show up until the 10th - 11th century, where as Michaelmas had been going strong since the 4th or 5th IIRC) I wish we had some actual record of the worship of Mabon in his pre-literary-figure form, but, tragically, we lack any.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T12:26:17-07:00","id":1409798,"title":"","content":"I think the issue with all that confusion is the fact that the pantheon was not a proper pantheon, but a collection of local gods with something in common. Honestly, most of what I found on the Nemetondevos (no I didn\u2019t look for that name) is the Interpretatio Romana of the gods, like Mars Teutatis and Mercurius Arvernus.<br /> <br /> To be fair, I don\u2019t have access to much of the most recent researches, other than a few references to Cernunnos, that apparently got a big revamp in the last few years, after a few centuries of misinterpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T12:29:29-07:00","id":1409799,"title":"","content":"By the way, my Asterix fan heart have to ask, where is Toutatis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T13:08:47-07:00","id":1409805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1408355-scion-homebrew-nemetondevos-revised?p=1409799#post1409799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, my Asterix fan heart have to ask, where is Toutatis?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Teutates is not a God; Lucan, the Roman poet, got it wrong. In truth, Teutates is a classification. He is not a God of the Tribes and a beacon of civilization across all continental and British Celtic peoples, they are a God of a Tribe, the patron of a specific tribal group. Almost all of the Nemetondevos are Teutates for different tribal groups, some patronizing a single tribe, others, entire tribal confederations. </div> </div> </div>It's all right there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Toutatis is just another way to spell Teutates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-22T14:01:23-07:00","id":1409815,"title":"","content":"Thank you a lot!<br /> \u201cFor Toutatis!\u201d still makes sense, a bit different, but a better one for sure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">P